$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of Hydroxysulfides-General
Procedure II SOCl2 (2 equiv.) was added dropwise to a solution of 2a, 2b,
or 2c (1 equiv.) in pyridine (1 equiv.). The reaction mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 1 h and then refluxed for an additional 1 h.
After cooling, water (50 mL) was added. The reaction mixture was then
extracted with CHCl3 (100 mL). The organic layer was washed with 35 mL of
aqueous NaOH (5%), with water (4 x 30 mL), and then dried over MgSO4. The
solvent was evaporated and the residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel with hexane as eluent. 3a [15], 3b, and 3c
were synthesized in the same way.
1,2,3,4,4-Pentachloro-1-(4-chlorobutylthio)-1,3-butadiene (3b) Compound
3b was synthesized from 2b (1.00 g, 3.024 mmol) according to the general
procedure II. The mixture was purified by column chromatography with
EtAc/petroleumther (1:2) as eluent. 3b: Yield: 0.93 g (88%); brown oil.
Rf = 0.61 (EtOAc/petroleum ether 1:2). IR (film): 2956, 2868 cm-1 (C-H),
1601, 1545 (C = C). 1H NMR: 1.56 (s, 2H, CH2CH2Cl), 1.90-1.96 (m, 2H,
SCH2CH2), 3.08-3.10 (m, 2H, SCH2), 3.54-3.59 (t, 2H, CH2Cl). Anal. calc.
for C8H8Cl6S (348.93): C, 27.54; H, 2.31, S 9.19 found C, 27.86; H, 2.13,
S 9.27.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
