$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Halogenation Conditions for Compounds
17-19. Into a 100 mL round-bottom flask were added the allylic alcohol
(5.05 mmol), N,N-diisopropylethylamine (1.41 mL, 8.09 mmol), and 30 mL of
dry acetonitrile. The solution was stirred at 0 °C for 10 min. Solid
dichlorotriphenylphosphorane (2.45 g, 7.58 mmol) was then added evenly to
the reaction mixture over a 7 min period. After the final addition of
Ph3PCl2, the reaction was allowed to stir at 0 °C for an additional 40
min. The mixture was then loaded directly onto a silica gel column and
purified by flash chromatography (5% EtOAc in hexane).
8-(p-Azido-N-ethyl-tetrafluoroaniline)-3,7-dimethyl-1-chloro-2,6-octadiene
(19). 1.74 g (85%) of a pale-yellow oil which rapidly turned orange. TLC:
(Rf 0.68).
