$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of Chlorine-Substituted Products
6a-6c. A mixture of 2 (1 mmol) and dry chloroform (10 mL) was stirred at
reflux. Then SOCl2 (5 mmol) was added to the solution, and the process
was monitored by TLC. After completion, to the solution was added the
corresponding alcoholic solvents (1 mL), then the solvent was removed by
vacuum, and the solid was further purified by silica gel column
chromatography (EtOAc) affording the pure products.
9b-Chloro-1-((6-chloropyridin-3-yl)methyl)-4a-methoxy-10-nitro-2,3,4a,9b-tetrahydroindeno[1′,2′:4,5]pyrrolo[1,2-a]imidazol-5(1H)-one
(6b). Yield, 85%. mp, 169.2-170.6 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 8.39
(s, 1H), 8.20 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.86 (d, J =
7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.82 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.69 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.52 (d,
J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 5.23 (d, J =15.8 Hz, 1H), 5.05 (d, J = 15.8 Hz, 1H),
3.97-4.10 (m, 1H), 3.77-3.97 (m, 2H), 3.67-3.77 (m, 1H), 3.43 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 189.0, 155.7, 149.8, 149.5, 149.1, 139.2,
137.1, 131.7, 131.3, 130.7, 128.3, 124.6, 124.2, 102.9, 91.8, 86.4, 54.2,
53.6, 48.6, 40.6; HRMS (ES+) calcd for C20H17 35Cl2N4O4 (M + H)+,
447.0627; found, 447.0622. Calcd for C20H17 35Cl 37ClN4O4 (M + H)+,
449.0597; found, 449.0597.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tetrahydroindeno[1',2':4,5]pyrrolo[1,2-a]imidazol-5(1H)-ones as Novel
Neonicotinoid Insecticides: Reaction Selectivity and Substituent Effects
on the Activity Level
