$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of α
-Chlorobenzylphosphonates from α -Hydroxyphosphonates. A solution of 1k
(1.00 g, 3.46 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and Ph3P (1.36 g, 5.19 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in
dry CCl4 (10 mL) is refluxed for 8 h under argon. Then, the mixture is
evaporated under reduced pressure, and the semisolid residue is extracted
with PE. The combined extracts are filtered, and the solvent is removed
under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel to yield 3k. Diethyl α
-chlorobenzylphosphonate (3a). Yield 85%. 1HNMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
1.17 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 1.32 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 3.85-3.93 (m, 1H),
4.02-4.06 (m, 1H), 4.07-4.23 (m, 2H), 4.91 (d, 2JPH = 14.1 Hz, 1H), 7.36
(d, J = 5.9 Hz, 3H), 7.53 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 16.3 (d, 3JPC = 5.8 Hz), 16.5 (d, 3JPC = 5.8 Hz), 53.7 (d,
1JPC = 158.7 Hz), 64.0 (d, 2JPC = 6.8 Hz), 64.1 (d, 2JPC = 7.2 Hz),
128.6, 129.0, 129.1, 134.2 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The first synthesis of diethyl α,α-chlorofluorobenzylphosphonates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wu, Di; He, Yanhong; Tang, Rongchang; Guan, Zhi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2009), (13), 2180-2182

