$DATUM Pyridine (2 mL) was added to a solution of lactone 1 (100 mg) in CHCl3
(15 mL) at 20 °C and then finally dispersed PCl5 (70 mg) was added
portion wise with continuous stirring. After 30 min. The reaction mixture
was washed with 5% HCl (15 mL) and then with water. The resulting
solution was dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was evaporated in vacuo.
Chromatography of the residue (a 3 : 1 lightpetroleum-Et2O mixture as the
eluent) afforded crystals of chlorolactone 5. Colorless crystals, yield
90 mg, 84%. m.p. 114--115 °C. [α]58022 +73.3°. UV, λmax/nm: 254 (ε
17100). IR, ν /cm-1: 1780 (γctone). 1687 (C(2)=O). 1640 and 1620 (two
cojugated C=C), 1261, 1224, 1196, 1179, 1009, 867. MS, m/z(lrel):
282[M+(37Cl)](33), 280 MS (35CI)] (100), 265 (5),245 (26), 244 (29), 217
(13), 201 (27), 199(21), 187 (21), 173 (33), 171 (71), 159 (27), 145
(23), 91 (39), 77(20), 44(22). Found, m/z: 280.08816, calculated for
C15H17ClO3: 280.08661 1H NMR. δ : 1.35 (d, 3 H, H3C(13). J11,13 = 7.6
Hz); 2.25 (br.s, 3 H, H3C{15}): 240 (brs, 3 H, H3C}: 2.70 (dd. 1 H,
H(9A), J8,9A = 6.0 Hz: J9A,9B = 15.0 Hz): 2,74 (br,dd. 1H, H(7), J7,11 =
7.6 Hz, J6,7 = 10.5 Hz): 2.81 (quiter, 1 H, 11). J7,11 = J11,12 = 7.6
Hz): 2.87 (br.d, 1 H, H(9B), J9A,9B = 15.0 Hz): 3.32 (d, 1 H. H(5), J5,6
= 10.5 Hz): 4.30 (t. 1 H, H(8) J5,6 = J6,7 = 10.5 Hz): 4.53 (brd. 1 H,
H(8), J8,9A = 6.0 Hz. J8,9B = 1 Hz): 6.13 (br.s. 1 H. H(3)). The data of
13C NHR spectroscopy are given in Table 1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
