$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Chlorine-Substituted Products 6a-6c. A mixture of 2 (1 mmol) and dry
chloroform (10 mL) was stirred at reflux. Then SOCl2 (5 mmol) was added
to the solution, and the process was monitored by TLC. After completion,
to the solution was added the corresponding alcoholic solvents (1 mL),
then the solvent was removed by vacuum, and the solid was further
purified by silica gel column chromatography (EtOAc) affording the pure
products.
9b-Chloro-1-((6-chloropyridin-3-yl)methyl)-4a-ethoxy-10-nitro-2,3,4a,9b-tetrahydroindeno[1′,2′:4,5]pyrrolo[1,2-a]imidazol-5(1H)-one
(6c). Yield, 83%. mp, 98.5-100.1 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 8.38
(d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 8.21 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.95-7.88 (m, 1H), 7.85
(d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.81 (dd, J 1 =2.4 Hz, J 2= 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (t, J
= 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.52 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 5.20 (d, J =15.8 Hz, 1H), 5.04
(d, J =15.8 Hz, 1H), 3.96-4.08 (m, 1H), 3.85-3.96 (m, 1H), 3.77-3.86 (m,
1H), 3.65-3.76 (m, 2H), 3.48-3.60 (m, 1H), 1.20 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 189.0, 155.6, 149.9, 149.5, 149.1, 139.2,
137.1, 131.7, 131.2, 130.6, 128.4, 124.5, 124.2, 103.7, 91.5, 86.5, 61.4,
54.2, 48.6, 40.6, 14.8; HRMS (ES+) calcd for C21H19 35Cl2N4O4 (M + H)+,
461.0783; found, 461.0779. Calcd for C21H19 35Cl 37ClN4O4 (M + H)+,
463.0754; found, 463.0750.
