$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1-Chloromethyl-2-methylpropyl)-carbamic acid benzyl ester:
2,4,6-Trichloro-[1,3,5]-triazine (1.83 g, 10.0 mmol) was added to DMF (2
mL), maintained at 25 °C. After the formation of a white solid, the
reaction was monitored (TLC) until complete disappearance of TCT, CH2Cl2
(25 mL) was added, followed by the alcohol (2.59 g, 9.5 mmol). After the
addition, the mixture was stirred at room temperature, monitored (TLC)
until completion (4 h). Water (20 mL) was added then the organic phase
washed with 15 mL of a saturated solution of Na2CO3, followed by 1 N HCl
and brine. The organic layer were dried (Na2SO4) and the solvent
evaporated. (S)(1-chloromethyl-2-methypropyl)-carbamic acid benzyl ester
that was isolated without other purifications (2.02 g, 83%). [α]20 D
-16.86 (c 3.2, CHCl3), 1H NMR δ 7.44 (s, 5H), 5.19 (s, 2H), 4.92 (d, 1Η),
4.31 (m, 1H), 3.86 (m, 2H), 1.95 (m, 1H), 1.04 (d, 6H); 13C NMR δ 161.4,
136.4, 128.7, 127.3, 66.9, 64.1, 55.1, 29.7, 19.3. Anal. Calcd. for
C13H18ClNO2 (255.74): C, 61.05; H, 7.09; Cl, 13.86; N, 5,48. Found C,
61.09, H, 7.09, Cl, 13.84, N, 5.46.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Route to Alkyl Chlorides from Alcohols Using the Complex
TCT/DMF
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM De Luca, Lidia; Giacomelli, Giampaolo; Porcheddu, Andrea
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(4), 553-555

