$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Experimental Procedure. Anhydrous
FeCl3 (8.1 mg, 0.05 mmol) in DME (5 mL) was added to a three-necked flask
with stirring at room temperature. When the color of the mixture turned
to deep blue, the carbonyl compound (1 mmol) and chlorosilane (1.1 mmol)
were added to the solution. The resulting mixture was refluxed for
indicated time (Table 2) until the disappearance of carbonyl compounds
(monitored by TLC). Then the mixture was cooled to room temperature,
quenched with dilute hydrochloric acid (0.3 M) and extracted with diethyl
ether (3 x 20 mL). The combined organic layer was washed with aqueous
NaHCO3 (10 mL) and saturated brine (20 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by
preparative TLC on silica gel with ethyl acetate and cyclohexane (1:8) as
eluent to afford pure products. Entry: 12, Cmpd: 2l, Yield: 83%. bp.: 35
(0.3 mm) °C, lit. bp.: 35 (0.3 mm) °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ferric chloride-catalyzed deoxygenative chlorination of carbonyl
compounds to halides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Z.; Sheng, C.; Qiu, H.; Zhang, Y.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2007), 39(4), 412-415

