$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Competitive Intermolecular Experiment between
Benzyl Alcohols and Aliphatic Alcohols: 4-Chlorobenzyl Chloride (Table 2,
Entry 6); Typical Procedure. The competitive intermolecular experiment
between 4-chlorobenzyl alcohol and 2-phenoxyethanol (Table 2, entry 6) is
representative. To a soln of 4-chlorobenzyl alcohol (444 mg, 3.12 mmol)
and 2-phenoxyethanol (431 mg, 3.12 mmol) in anhyd DMSO (5 mL) was added
TCT (316 mg, 1.71 mmol) portionwise. The reaction mixture was stirred at
r.t. for 25 min and then Et2O (50 mL) was added. The organic phase was
washed with H2O (5 × 30 mL), dried over anhyd Na2SO4 and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The mixture was separated by silica gel
chromatography with petroleum ether to give 4-chlorobenzyl chloride.
Table 2, Entry 7: Yield 78%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A highly chemoselective and rapid chlorination of benzyl alcohols under
neutral conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
