$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 5a-5d: A mixture of 2 (1 mmol) and the
corresponding alcoholic solvents (10 mL) was stirred at room temperature.
Then, TsOH (0.1 mmol) was added to the solution, and the process was
monitored by TLC. After completion, the solvent was removed by vacuum,
and dry tetrahydrofuran (10 mL) was added. Then, NaH (1.5 mmol) was added
to the solution until no bubbles were produced, then the corresponding
alkyl iodide (5 mmol) was added. The process was monitored by TLC. After
completion, the solvent was removed by vacuum, and the solid was further
purified by silica gel column chromatography (EtOAc) affording the pure
products.
9b-Chloro-1-((6-chloropyridin-3-yl)methyl)-4a-hydroxy-10-nitro-2,3,4a,9b-tetrahydroindeno[1′,2′:4,5]pyrrolo[1,2-a]imidazol-5(1H)-one
(6a). Yield, 82%. mp, 170.3-170.7 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 8.37
(s, 1H), 8.28 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.93 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.83 (d, J =
7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.80 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.66 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.53 (d,
J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.21 (s, 1H), 5.34 (d, J =15.6 Hz, 1H), 4.86 (d, J =15.6
Hz, 1H), 3.91-4.02 (m, 1H), 3.82-3.90 (m, 1H), 3.57-3.75 (m, 2H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 189.4, 154.6, 151.6, 149.6, 149.2, 139.3, 137.5,
131.7, 130.8, 130.4, 128.0, 124.4, 124.2, 106.6, 88.8, 86.6, 53.8, 48.3,
40.1; HRMS (ES+) calcd for C19H15 35Cl2N4O4 (M + H)+, 433.0470; found,
433.0462. Calcd for C19H15 35Cl 37C37ClN4O4 (M + H)+, 435.0441; found,
435.0430.
