$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3,7-Bis(chloromethyl)-5H-dibenzo[b,d]thiophene-5,5-dione (IV). A mixture
of 3,7-bis-(hydroxymethyl)-dibenzothiophene-5,5-dione I (2.76 g, 1.0
mmol), 10 ml of toluene, and 0.5 ml (∼7 mmol, 3.5 eq.) of thionyl
chloride were refluxed till HCl stopped releasing. The solvent was
evacuated with the rotor evaporator; the residue was dissolved in 50 ml
of hexane and purified by flash-chromatography.
3,7-Bis(chloromethyl)-1-hexyloxy-5H-dibenzo[b,d]thiophene-5,5-dione (VI)
was prepared similarly, from 1-hexyloxy derivative (III) and thionyl
chloride. Yield 3.76 g (82%). mp 44-46°C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 2985,
2950, 2875, 1605, 1590, 1500, 1465, 1410, 1370, 1305, 1275, 1170, 1045,
935, 895, 870, 720. Found, %: C 57.84; H 5.14. C20H22Cl2O3S. Calculated,
%: C 58.11; H 5.36. M 413.37. 1H NMR, (DMSO-d6), δ, ppm
5,5-dioxodibenzothiophene: 0.87 t (3H, CH3, J 7 Hz), 1.29-1.32 m (4H,
(CH2)2, 1.46 m (2H, CH2), 1.83 m (2H, CH2), 4.08 s (2H, OCH2), 4.84 s
(2H, CH2), 4.86 s (2H, CH2), 7.53 s (1H, H2), 7.58 s (1H, H4), 7.82 d.d
(1H, H8, J 1.5, 8.5 Hz), 8.02 s (1H, H6), 8.21 d (1H, H9, J 8.5 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and fungicidal activity of the quaternary ammonium salts of the
1,3,7-substituted dibenzothiophene-5,5-diones
