$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ethyl
1-Aryl-4-chloromethyl-1H-pyrazole-3-carboxylates 3a-d (General Method).
SOCl2 (3.6 g, 0.03 mol) was added with stirring to a solution of ester
2a-d (0.02 mol) in CH2Cl2 (40 ml), stirred at room temperature for 2 h,
and then for 1 h at 40°C. The mixture was cooled, solvent and excess
SOCl2 were distilled off, and the residue was washed with hexane (2x30ml)
and crystallized from EtOH Compound 3d, yield80%. Empirical formula :
C13H11Cl3N2O2. Found, % : Calculated, % C 46.55/ 46.81. H 3.10 /3.32. N :
8.27/ 8.40. Mp, °С : 150-151. IR spectrum, ν , cm-1 С=О: 1725 . ОН (NH)*2
:-. 1Н NMR spectrum, δ , ppm (J, Hz): 1.35 (3Н, t, J = 6.5, CH2СН3); 4.36
(2Н, q, J = 6.5, CH2СН3); 4.90 (2Н, s, СН2Cl); 7.81-7.94 (2Н, m, Н Ar);
8.24 (1Н, d, J = 1.5, Н Ar); 8.88 (1Н, s, Н -5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM excess SOCl2 used
