$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3,7-Bis(chloromethyl)-5H-dibenzo[b,d]thiophene-5,5-dione (IV). A mixture
of 3,7-bis-(hydroxymethyl)-dibenzothiophene-5,5-dione I (2.76 g, 1.0
mmol), 10 ml of toluene, and 0.5 ml (∼7 mmol, 3.5 eq.) of thionyl
chloride were refluxed till HCl stopped releasing. The solvent was
evacuated with the rotor evaporator; the residue was dissolved in 50 ml
of hexane and purified by flash-chromatography.
3,7-Bis(chloromethyl)-1-methoxy-5H-dibenzo[b,d]thiophene-5,5-dione (V)
was prepared similarly, from
3,7-bis(hydroxymethyl)-1-methoxy-5H-dibenzo[b,d]thiophene-5,5-dione (II)
and thionyl chloride. Yield 3.06 g (77%). mp 176-178°C. IR spectrum, ν,
cm-1: 2990, 2960, 2880, 1610, 1590, 1500, 1465, 1415, 1370, 1305, 1270,
1160, 1055, 935, 895, 875, 730. Found, %: C 52.41; H 3.42. C15H12Cl2O3S.
Calculated, %: C 52.49; H 3.53. M 343.24. 1H NMR, (DMSO-d6), δ, ppm
5,5-dioxodibenzothiophene: 4.05 s (3H, OCH3), 4.84 s (2H, CH2), 4.86 s
(2H, CH2), 7.53 s (1H H2), 7.60 s (1H, H4), 7.81 d (1H, H8, J 1.5, 8.5
Hz), 8.01 s (1H, H6), 8.27 d (1H, H9).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and fungicidal activity of the quaternary ammonium salts of the
1,3,7-substituted dibenzothiophene-5,5-diones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
