$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Chlorocyclohexanone (3p)[6] Cyclohexanol (50 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv)
and TEMPO (8 mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.1 equiv) were dissolved in DCM (5 mL). TCCA
(116 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was then added in small portions. After
stirring for 10 min at rt, MeOH (32 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2.0 equiv) was added
dropwise. The reaction was stirred at rt, monitored by TLC and then
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude reaction mixture was
directly purified by FC on silica gel (pentane/DCM 1:1). The title
compound was isolated. Colorless oil, yield (50 mg, 75%). 1H NMR(300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 4.37 (ddd, J = 8.8, 5.1, 1.3 Hz, 1H, CHCl), 2.85 - 2.71 (m, 1H,
CHH), 2.44 - 2.27 (m, 2H), 2.13 - 1.60 (m, 5H); 13C NMR(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
203.52 (CO), 62.94 (CHCl), 39.48 (CH2), 37.52 (CH2), 27.17 (CH2), 22.97
(CH2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct Conversion of Alcohols to α-Chloro Aldehydes and α-Chloro Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jing, Yuanyuan; Daniliuc, Constantin G.; Studer, Armido
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(18), 4932-4935

