$DATUM 60-29-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-(1-Chloroalkyl)furans (general procedure). To a solution of 0.05 mol of
appropriate secondary alcohol and 0.05 mol of pyridine in 50 ml of
absolute ether, a solution of 0.05 mol of thionyl chloride in 10 m l of
absolute ether was added dropwise with stirring at 10-20°C. The mixture
was kept for 4 h at 15-20°C ; pyridine hydrochloride was filtered off and
washed with ether. The combined ether solution was evaporated in a
water-jet-pump vacuum, and the residue was distilled in a vacuum.
3-(1-Chloroethyl)furan I. Yield 75%. Because of fast formation of the gel
fraction in solutions, no properly resolved 1H NMR spectrum could be
obtained. bp 28°C (2 mm Hg).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 3-Chloroalkylfurans in the reaction with sodium diethyl phosphite
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pevzner, L. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2006), 76(8), 1299-1303

