$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3-(1-Chloroalkyl)furans (general procedure).
To a solution of 0.05 mol of appropriate secondary alcohol and 0.05 mol
of pyridine in 50 ml of absolute ether, a solution of 0.05 mol of thionyl
chloride in 10 m l of absolute ether was added dropwise with stirring at
10-20°C. The mixture was kept for 4 h at 15-20°C ; pyridine hydrochloride
was filtered off and washed with ether. The combined ether solution was
evaporated in a water-jet-pump vacuum, and the residue was distilled in a
vacuum. 3-(1-Chloroethyl)-5-methylfuran II. Yield 74%. bp 23-24°C (1 mm
Hg). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, pm: 1.784 d (CH3-chloroethyl, J HH 6.4 Hz),
2.268 s (CH3-furan), 5.035 q (CHCl, J HH 6.4 Hz), 6.072 s (H4-furan),
7.259 s (H2-furan).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 3-Chloroalkylfurans in the reaction with sodium diethyl phosphite
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pevzner, L. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2006), 76(8), 1299-1303

