$DATUM Compound 5. To a solution of 0.89 g (2.6 mmol) of 4 and 4.17 mL (30 mmol)
of triethylamine in 5 mL of CH2Cl2 was added 2.93 mL (30 mmol) of
methanesulfonyl chloride at 0 °C, followed by 0.24 g (2 mmol) of DMAP.
The mixture was stirred overnight at ambient temperature, diluted with
CH2Cl2, and washed with 1N HCl, saturated NaHCO3 solution, and brine. The
combined organic phases were dried and concentrated. Flash chromatography
on silica gel furnished 678 mg (72%) of 5 as a pale yellow oil. Compound
5, yield 678 mg, 72% IR (neat, cm-1) 1747,1705, 1618; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
C6D6) δ 5.40-5.22 (m, 2 H), 3.23 (dd, J = 8.9, 8.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.72 (d, J =
6.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.18-2.05 (m, 1 H), 1.90-1.79 (m, 1 H), 1.70-1.55 (m, 1 H),
1.45-1.25 (m, 2 H), 1.21 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 3 H), 1.20 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 3 H),
1.11 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 3 H), 1.10 (s, 3 H), 1.07 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 3 H), 0.75
(5,3 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, C6D6) δ 215.0, 196.5, 165.5, 131.6, 74.4, 73.5,
72.3, 60.2, 59.5, 47.4, 42.5, 42.2, 32.6, 25.3, 23.4, 22.8, 22.6, 22.5,
22.4; MS FAB m/z cal cd for C19H27ClO4+ 354.16, obsd 354.12. Anal. Calcd
for C19H27ClO4: C, 64.31; H, 7.67. Found:C, 64.40; H, 7.55.
