$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedures for the Halogenation of
Benzyl alcohols 4-Fluoro-2-phenylbenzyl chloride (Table 2, entry 9); 71%.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.45-7.36 (m, 5H), 7.27-7.23 (m, 2H), 7.07 (m,
1H), 4.48 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.3 (d, 1 J C-F = 245.3
Hz), 139.8, 137.9 (d, 4 J C-F = 3.1 Hz), 136.9 (d,3 J C-F = 7.5 Hz),
131.8 (d, 3JC-F = 8.2 Hz), 129.1, 128.3, 127.6, 116.8, 136.9 (d, 2 J C-F
= 21.8 Hz), 115.5 (d, 3 J C-F = 21.0 Hz), 43.7; IR (Film) ν 3061, 2738,
1844, 1653, 1540, 1507, 1418, 1273, 1010, 964, 826 cm-1; HRMS (EI+) m/z
calcd. for C13H10ClF [M]+: 220.0456, found: 220.0455.
